IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ss-types`
IMPORT `ss-general`
IMPORT `ss-rates`
IMPORT `ss-entitlement`
IMPORT `ss-commencement`
IMPORT `ss-goal`

-- Social Security Act 2018, main benefits — THE ENCODER'S TESTS.
--
-- Expected values are worked by hand from the Act's text. Jobseeker support
-- is tested with an assumed base rate of $337.74 subject to Income Test 3
-- (both are inputs; the table is lost in the converted text).

§ `Tests`

§§ `Income tests and rates`

#ASSERT `the reduction under` `Income Test 1` `on weekly income of` 160 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the reduction under` `Income Test 1` `on weekly income of` 200 EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `the reduction under` `Income Test 1` `on weekly income of` 250 EQUALS 27
#ASSERT `the reduction under` `Income Test 1` `on weekly income of` 300 EQUALS 62
#ASSERT `the reduction under` `Income Test 2` `on weekly income of` 300 EQUALS 31
#ASSERT `the reduction under` `Income Test 3` `on weekly income of` 300 EQUALS 98
#ASSERT `the reduction under` `Income Test 4` `on weekly income of` 300 EQUALS 49
#ASSERT `the reduction under` `Income Test 3` `on weekly income of` 100 EQUALS 0

GIVEN income IS A NUMBER, childcare IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Rate facts`
rate income childcare MEANS `Rate facts` OF 337.74, `Income Test 3`, income, childcare

#ASSERT `the weekly rate of` `sole parent support` `, rate facts` (rate 0 0) EQUALS 521.52
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of` `sole parent support` `, rate facts` (rate 300 0) EQUALS 459.52
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of` `sole parent support` `, rate facts` (rate 200 20) EQUALS 515.52
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of` `sole parent support` `, rate facts` (rate 200 30) EQUALS 515.52
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of` `sole parent support` `, rate facts` (rate 1000 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of` `jobseeker support` `, rate facts` (rate 100 0) EQUALS 337.74
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of` `jobseeker support` `, rate facts` (rate 300 0) EQUALS 239.74
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of` `jobseeker support` `, rate facts` (rate 700 0) EQUALS 0

§§ `General requirements (ss 16, 18, 19)`

GIVEN dob IS A DATE, status IS AN `Immigration status`, years IS A NUMBER, refugee IS A BOOLEAN, reciprocity IS A NUMBER, other IS A BOOLEAN, child IS A BOOLEAN, situation IS A `Relationship situation`
GIVETH AN Applicant
person dob status years refugee reciprocity other child situation MEANS
    Applicant OF dob, status, TRUE, years, refugee, reciprocity GREATER THAN 0, reciprocity, other, child, situation

adult MEANS person (Date 1 1 2000) `a New Zealand citizen` 5 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE `single`
today MEANS Date 16 10 2026

#ASSERT `meets the residential requirement` adult
#ASSERT NOT `meets the residential requirement` (person (Date 1 1 2000) `a New Zealand citizen` 1.9 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE `single`)
#ASSERT `meets the residential requirement` (person (Date 1 1 2000) `a residence class visa holder` 0.5 TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE `single`)
#ASSERT `meets the residential requirement` (person (Date 1 1 2000) `a temporary entry class visa holder` 0 FALSE 2 FALSE FALSE `single`)
#ASSERT NOT `meets the residential requirement` (person (Date 1 1 2000) `a temporary entry class visa holder` 0 FALSE 1.5 FALSE FALSE `single`)
#ASSERT NOT `meets the residential requirement` (person (Date 1 1 2000) `a temporary entry class visa holder` 5 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE `single`)
#ASSERT `is barred by ss 18 or 19` (person (Date 1 1 2000) `a temporary entry class visa holder` 0 FALSE 2 FALSE FALSE `single`)
#ASSERT `is barred by ss 18 or 19` (person (Date 1 1 2000) `a New Zealand citizen` 5 FALSE 0 TRUE FALSE `single`)
#ASSERT NOT `is barred by ss 18 or 19` adult

§§ `Jobseeker support (ss 20-26)`

GIVEN employed IS A BOOLEAN, available IS A BOOLEAN, student IS A BOOLEAN, strike IS A BOOLEAN, temporary IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Jobseeker facts`
js employed available student strike temporary MEANS `Jobseeker facts` OF employed, FALSE, available, student, strike, FALSE, temporary

seeker MEANS js FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `is entitled to jobseeker support` adult seeker (rate 0 0) today
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to jobseeker support` adult (js TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (rate 0 0) today
#ASSERT `is entitled to jobseeker support` adult (`Jobseeker facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) (rate 0 0) today
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to jobseeker support` adult (js FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) (rate 0 0) today
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to jobseeker support` (person (Date 17 10 2008) `a New Zealand citizen` 5 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE `single`) seeker (rate 0 0) today
#ASSERT `is entitled to jobseeker support` (person (Date 16 10 2008) `a New Zealand citizen` 5 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE `single`) seeker (rate 0 0) today
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to jobseeker support` (person (Date 1 1 2007) `a New Zealand citizen` 5 FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE `single`) seeker (rate 0 0) today
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to jobseeker support` adult (js FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) (rate 0 0) today
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to jobseeker support` adult (js FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) (rate 0 0) today
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to jobseeker support` adult seeker (rate 700 0) today
#ASSERT `is entitled to jobseeker support` adult (js FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) (rate 700 0) today

§§ `Sole parent support (ss 29-33)`

GIVEN caring IS A BOOLEAN, split IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sole parent facts`
sp caring split MEANS `Sole parent facts` OF caring, JUST (Date 1 3 2015), split

#ASSERT `is entitled to sole parent support` adult (sp TRUE FALSE) today
#ASSERT `is entitled to sole parent support` adult (sp TRUE FALSE) (Date 28 2 2029)
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to sole parent support` adult (sp TRUE FALSE) (Date 1 3 2029)
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to sole parent support` adult (sp FALSE FALSE) today
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to sole parent support` adult (sp TRUE TRUE) today
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to sole parent support` (person (Date 1 1 2000) `a New Zealand citizen` 5 FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE `with a supporting spouse or partner`) (sp TRUE FALSE) today
#ASSERT `is entitled to sole parent support` (person (Date 1 1 2000) `a New Zealand citizen` 5 FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE `living apart and unsupported or inadequately maintained`) (sp TRUE FALSE) today
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to sole parent support` (person (Date 1 1 2007) `a New Zealand citizen` 5 FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE `single`) (sp TRUE FALSE) today

§§ `Supported living payment (ss 34-40)`

GIVEN permanent IS A BOOLEAN, hours IS A NUMBER, blind IS A BOOLEAN, self IS A BOOLEAN, carer IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Supported living facts`
slp permanent hours blind self carer MEANS `Supported living facts` OF permanent, hours, TRUE, blind, self, carer, FALSE

#ASSERT `is entitled to the supported living payment for restricted work capacity or blindness` adult (slp TRUE 14 FALSE FALSE FALSE) today
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to the supported living payment for restricted work capacity or blindness` adult (slp TRUE 15 FALSE FALSE FALSE) today
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to the supported living payment for restricted work capacity or blindness` adult (slp FALSE 5 FALSE FALSE FALSE) today
#ASSERT `is entitled to the supported living payment for restricted work capacity or blindness` adult (slp FALSE 40 TRUE FALSE FALSE) today
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to the supported living payment for restricted work capacity or blindness` adult (slp TRUE 0 FALSE TRUE FALSE) today
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to the supported living payment for restricted work capacity or blindness` (person (Date 17 10 2010) `a New Zealand citizen` 5 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE `single`) (slp TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) today
#ASSERT `is entitled to the supported living payment for restricted work capacity or blindness` (person (Date 16 10 2010) `a New Zealand citizen` 5 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE `single`) (slp TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE FALSE) today
#ASSERT `is entitled to the supported living payment for caring` adult (slp FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE) today
-- s 40(1)(a) (added after the independent pass): not for caring for one's own
-- spouse or partner.
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to the supported living payment for caring` adult (`Supported living facts` OF FALSE, 40, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) today
#ASSERT NOT `is entitled to the supported living payment for caring` (person (Date 1 1 2007) `a New Zealand citizen` 5 FALSE 0 FALSE TRUE `single`) (slp FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE) today
#ASSERT `is entitled to the supported living payment for caring` (person (Date 1 1 2007) `a New Zealand citizen` 5 FALSE 0 FALSE FALSE `single`) (slp FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE TRUE) today

§§ `Commencement (s 316)`

GIVEN ceased IS A MAYBE DATE, applied IS A DATE, days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Commencement facts`
start ceased applied days MEANS `Commencement facts` OF Date 1 10 2026, ceased, applied, days, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `the day the benefit commences, benefit` `jobseeker support` `, facts` (start NOTHING (Date 5 10 2026) 7) EQUALS Date 8 10 2026
#ASSERT `the day the benefit commences, benefit` `jobseeker support` `, facts` (start NOTHING (Date 20 10 2026) 7) EQUALS Date 20 10 2026
#ASSERT `the day the benefit commences, benefit` `sole parent support` `, facts` (start NOTHING (Date 20 10 2026) 7) EQUALS Date 8 10 2026
#ASSERT `the day the benefit commences, benefit` `sole parent support` `, facts` (start NOTHING (Date 29 10 2026) 7) EQUALS Date 8 10 2026
-- Changed after the independent pass (fork F1): sole parent support applied
-- for 29 days after entitlement is refused, as s 316 gives no rule; the old
-- assertion (30 October) is removed rather than asserted, since a refusal
-- cannot be asserted equal to anything.
#ASSERT `the day the benefit commences, benefit` `jobseeker support` `, facts` (start (JUST (Date 3 10 2026)) (Date 5 10 2026) 7) EQUALS Date 11 10 2026
-- s 316(1)(a)(ii) (added after the independent pass): employment that ended
-- only after applying does not move the start.
#ASSERT `the day the benefit commences, benefit` `jobseeker support` `, facts` (`Commencement facts` OF Date 1 10 2026, JUST (Date 10 10 2026), Date 5 10 2026, 7, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS Date 8 10 2026
#ASSERT `the day the benefit commences, benefit` `supported living payment for caring for another person` `, facts` (start NOTHING (Date 5 10 2026) 0) EQUALS Date 1 10 2026
#ASSERT `the day the benefit commences, benefit` `jobseeker support` `, facts` (`Commencement facts` OF Date 1 10 2026, NOTHING, Date 20 10 2026, 7, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS Date 8 10 2026

§§ `The top-level goal`

#ASSERT `the benefit position for` `sole parent support` `, applicant` adult `, jobseeker facts` seeker `, sole parent facts` (sp TRUE FALSE) `, supported living facts` (slp FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE) `, rate facts` (rate 300 0) `, commencement facts` (start NOTHING (Date 5 10 2026) 7) EQUALS `Benefit position` OF TRUE, 459.52, JUST (Date 8 10 2026)
#ASSERT `the benefit position for` `sole parent support` `, applicant` adult `, jobseeker facts` seeker `, sole parent facts` (sp FALSE FALSE) `, supported living facts` (slp FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE) `, rate facts` (rate 300 0) `, commencement facts` (start NOTHING (Date 5 10 2026) 7) EQUALS `Benefit position` OF FALSE, 0, NOTHING
#ASSERT `the benefit position for` `jobseeker support` `, applicant` adult `, jobseeker facts` seeker `, sole parent facts` (sp FALSE FALSE) `, supported living facts` (slp FALSE 40 FALSE FALSE FALSE) `, rate facts` (rate 300 0) `, commencement facts` (start NOTHING (Date 20 10 2026) 7) EQUALS `Benefit position` OF TRUE, 239.74, JUST (Date 20 10 2026)
